==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[criticise]] (''UK'')

===Etymology===
Century 1911: < {{suffix|critic|ize}}

From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κριτικός|tr=kritikos|sc=polytonic||of or for judging, able to discern}} < {{term|κρίσις|tr=krisis|sc=polytonic||crisis}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|criticizes|criticizing|criticized}}  (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')

# to [[evaluate]] (something), and [[judge]] its [[merit]]s and [[fault]]s
# to [[find fault]] (with something)

